-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Hongyuan</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Studies of micelle and trace non-polar organic solvent on a new chemiluminescence system and its application to flow injection analysis</article-title><source>Anal Chim Acta</source><year>2000</year><volume>409</volume><fpage>75</fpage><lpage>81</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0003-2670(99)00856-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Afsaneh</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohammad</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Flow injection determination of cationic surfactants by using <italic>N</italic>-bromosuccinimide and <italic>N</italic>-chlorosuccinimide as new oxidizing agents for luminol chemiluminescence</article-title><source>Anal Chim Acta</source><year>2002</year><volume>468</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>63</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0003-2670(02)00592-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haiyan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Review of the application of non-ionic surfactants</article-title><source>Chin J Prac Tech</source><year>1997</year><fpage>24</fpage><lpage>25</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jason</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Karen</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mark</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Enhanced electrochemiluminescence from Os(phen)<sub>2</sub>(dppene)<sup>2+ </sup>(phen=1,10-phenanthroline and dppene=bis(diphenylphosphino)ethene) in the presence of Triton X-100 (polyethylene glycol tert-octylphenyl ether)</ar